{"name":"Atelier","hex":"#a3abb8","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"atelier","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A studio or workshop, especially for an artist, designer, or fashion house."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/atelier"}],"entries":[{"title":"Atelier","blocks":[{"text":"An atelier is the private workshop or studio of a professional artist in the fine or decorative arts or an architect, where a principal master and a number of assistants, students, and apprentices can work together producing fine art or visual art released under the master's name or supervision."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b5/%C3%89cole_des_beaux-arts_%28from_the_live%29.jpg/330px-%C3%89cole_des_beaux-arts_%28from_the_live%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atelier"},{"title":"Atelier (video game series)","blocks":[{"text":"The Atelier series is a franchise of bishoujo role-playing video games developed by Gust Corporation since 1997, originally being primarily for the PlayStation line of consoles. Main entries in the series have seen consistent releases for Microsoft Windows since 2015 and the Nintendo Switch since 2017. New games are released in the series on an almost yearly basis. The series was solely released in Japan and Asia until 2004, after which the series has seen worldwide releases."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/7c/Atelier_%28video_game_series%29_logo.png/330px-Atelier_%28video_game_series%29_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atelier_(video_game_series)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Bashkirtseff_-_In_the_Studio.jpg/500px-Bashkirtseff_-_In_the_Studio.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/